<tr><td>Robot</td><td>Pose <b>holding</b>; the arm hangs under Hex's first bubble. From line 2 on, the <b>target box lights up</b> (<code>showHint</code> glow) with the label <b>"TARGET AREA"</b> and stays lit to the end.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hex lines</td><td>1. "The robot is holding the cube." (above the arm, row top 182). 2. "The target area is marked on the table." (at the bottom of the artboard, just under the target box so it never covers what it points at; 69 px below the artboard's bottom). 3. "Let's move the cube in the target area!" (above the button, 118 px).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bubble</td><td>167 px wide, typed letter by letter.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Transition between lines</td><td>On Continue the bubble <b>bounces and flies off left</b>, Hex follows and slides off; after 350 ms the next line enters at its new place with a fresh Hex entrance. The button is locked during this.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Continue" for all three lines. After the last, goes to step 8.</td></tr>
</table>

