<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Next". Goes to step 10.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ---------- Screen 10 -->
<h3>Screen 10: Flip the card to reveal. (<code>/module?step=10</code>)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Background</td><td><b>RoomBackdrop</b>: <code>flipCard-bg.svg</code>, an empty room cropped to the 390 x 844 frame, covering the whole stage. Where cropped, it is held on the horizon at 67% of the height.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Card</td><td>The "Flip card" artboard (207 x 275) of <code>progressBar.riv</code>, state machine <code>Card_SM</code>, drawn 350 px tall in the middle of the stage. Both faces are drawn by the artboard (front: "Tap to reveal").</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bleed</td><td>Canvas is 20 artboard units larger on every side so the swell of the turn is not clipped by the artboard edge.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Enter</td><td>Hidden until the Rive file loads (button disabled), then fades in and springs up from 40 px below (stiffness 140, damping 16). The file is preloaded with matching CORS mode so it is not downloaded twice.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Interaction</td><td>Each tap fires the <code>Trigger 1</code> flip trigger (turns the card over, and back on the next tap), plays the click sound, haptic tap and press scale 0.98.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Next" - disabled until the card has been turned once. Goes to step 11.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ---------- Screen 11 -->
<h3>Screen 11: Instructions are... (<code>/module?step=11</code>)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Quiz: what instructions are known as. Correct = Command.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shell</td><td>Level One shell with <code>wash</code> (blue gradient) and <code>fit</code> (shrinks to avoid scrolling).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Title row</td><td>Teal-tinted 52 px badge with a "Q" image and "<i>Instructions</i> are..." (28 px). Enters from 60 px above with opacity and a spring (delayed 0.3 s).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hex</td><td>Large (1.1x his slot) in a 180 x 177 slot above the options, drawn by <code>HexGlide</code> (see below).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Options</td><td>Three rows 89 px tall, 12 px radius, with a 4 px bottom edge: <b>Statement</b> (lavender), <b>Command</b> (pink <code>#FFF4F6</code>, correct), <b>Question</b> (cream). Image 33 to 48 px + 20 px label.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Option enter</td><td>Drop-in effect (<code>optionDropIn</code>).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Press</td><td>Row sinks onto its 4 px edge (<code>active:border-b-0</code>, scale 0.97, y +4).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Select</td><td>Card bounces in 3D: scale [1, 0.93, 1.07, 0.99, 1] and rotateX [0, 14, -8, 3, 0] over 0.55 s, perspective 600 px; edge and fill turn green.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wrong pick</td><td>Red edge/fill and a red circle with a white X pops in at the row's right (scale 0 &rarr; 1, 200 ms).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hint</td><td>Hinted card does the 2-turn flip and float; once the flip is done, <b>Hex flies from the question slot to a spot on top of the Command card</b> (small, 72 px) with a quicker well damped spring (stiffness 170, damping 24).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Check</td><td>Question slot closes (height 177 &rarr; 0) on the result panel's spring (360 / 32) so the options rise as the panel arrives, as if pushed. Hex stays put and sinks under the options (<code>rising</code>, z-5, ride down 37 px), while the panel brings its own Hex.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Panel text</td><td>Right: "Yes! Instructions in a program is called <b>commands.</b>" Wrong: "Remember: Instructions in a program are called <b>commands.</b>" Default titles (Correct! / Not quite).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Right extras</td><td>Confetti + "+10 XP". Panel Hex thumbs-up.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Next</td><td>Continue goes via <code>nextAfter</code> to step 12 (Level 1's 3rd screen).</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ---------- Screen 12 and 13 -->
<h3>Screen 12: Imagine Teacher Says.. (<code>/module?step=12</code>) and Screen 13: What teacher is doing? (<code>/module?step=13</code>)</h3>
<p>Both are the <b>same mounted component</b> (<code>TeacherFlow</code>) with a step of "says" or "quiz", so moving between them keeps the teacher picture on screen and animates it. Browser Back/Forward move the URL and the screen follows; tapping moves the screen first and the URL after.</p>

<h4>Screen 12 (says)</h4>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Heading</td><td>"<i>Imagine</i> Teacher Says.." as <b>karaoke text</b>: fills in as the voice reads "Let Suppose Teacher Says" (word times 0.14-0.83, 1.47-1.8, 1.8-2.17 s of the 4.03 s clip <code>screen_3_audio.mpeg</code>). Cross-fades with the quiz heading in 0.3 s.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Picture</td><td><code>teacher-says.png</code> in an 8 px rounded box, 358 px tall (11 px below the title), cropped from the bottom on the quiz.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hex</td><td>Starts <b>below the picture</b> (spot 114,362; enters from 114,420, rising in) while the voice introduces it. About 2.8 s after the voice starts (or 6 s with no voice) he glides up beside the teacher (spot 228,84) on a slow soft spring (stiffness 70, damping 16) and then <b>floats</b> up and down 7 px every 2.4 s (starting 1.2 s later).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Speech bubble</td><td>White 18 px rounded bubble at the top right of the picture with orange quote marks. It pops in (scale 0.8 &rarr; 1, 0.25 s, delayed 350 ms) and the line "Open Your Notebook" is typed in, letter by letter. The bubble is sized by the full invisible line.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Continue". Moves to the quiz at once (picture morphs) and the URL becomes step 13.</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>Screen 13 (quiz)</h4>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Heading</td><td>"<i>What</i> teacher is doing?"</td></tr>
<tr><td>Picture morph</td><td>Picture crops from 358 to <b>240 px</b> tall with Hex and the bubble kept, over 0.8 s with ease [0.65, 0, 0.35, 1]. On check it crops further to 110 px on the panel's spring so the options ride up.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Question audio</td><td><code>screen_4_audio_trim.m4a</code> (just the question), read once until checked. Hex talks while it plays. Options are not read.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Options</td><td>Two cards 221 px tall, 19 px apart, 116 px picture: <b>Asking Question</b> (lavender) and <b>Giving Instruction</b> (cream, correct). They rise in 90 px with a spring after 0.3 s and exit 24 px down in 0.25 s if the screen steps back.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Select</td><td>Bounce [1, 0.95, 1.05, 1]; press 0.96; green or red looks as other quizzes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hint</td><td>Card does the 2-turn flip and float with an orange glow; <b>Hex flies to the top of the card</b> (small, 80/130 scale) when the flip finishes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Check</td><td>Hex <b>sinks behind the options</b> (spot 228,200 on the panel spring) as they rise; the panel brings its own Hex.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Panel text</td><td>"Yes! The teacher is giving an <b>instruction.</b>" or "Remember: The teacher is giving an <b>instruction.</b>"</td></tr>
<tr><td>Right extras</td><td>Confetti + "+10 XP".</td></tr>
<tr><td>Back</td><td>Back to the says view (the quiz restarts fresh: selection, hint, flip, checked and the bar's answer all reset).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Next</td><td>Continue goes to step 14.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ---------- Screen 14 -->
<h3>Screen 14: Examples of instruction (<code>/module?step=14</code>)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Heading</td><td>"<i>Examples</i> of instruction" as karaoke text read by the voice heading clip.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Voiceover</td><td>7 clips in order: heading, then for Parent, Coach and Traffic a left line and a right line each (<code>screen5_*_audio.m4a</code>). While the voice reads an example's two lines, that card is centred and the carousel does not auto-advance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Band</td><td>Full stage width, tinted <code>#04ACAB</code> at 12% (dark 30%) and <b>fading out to the top and bottom</b> with a mask gradient (transparent, black 30%, black 70%, transparent). Height = 382 + 32 + 86 px; centred between heading and button.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cards</td><td>Three cards 215 x 382 px (about 1:1.78), radius 18 px, soft teal drop shadow <code>0 14px 22px rgba(4,172,171,.28)</code>: Parent eats the food, Coach gives a command, Traffic signal says stop.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Carousel layout</td><td>Active card centred (scale 1, brightness 1, z-index 1). Neighbours at +/-113 px, 14 px lower, scale 0.88, <b>rotated 4 degrees</b> in/out (rotate = slot x 4), opacity 0.85, brightness 0.9. Loops forever.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Move animation</td><td>0.9 s with ease [0.32, 0.72, 0, 1].</td></tr>
<tr><td>Controls</td><td>Swipe or drag (offset over 50 px or velocity over 400, rubber band 0.2, snap back); tap a neighbour; arrow keys; tap a pagination bar.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Auto-advance</td><td>Moves on every 3.6 s unless held (touching) or the voice is speaking. Off for reduced-motion users.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pagination</td><td>3 pills; the active one is wider (24 px vs 12 px, 500 ms) and carries a <b>countdown fill</b> that grows across it over 3.6 s (linear) and restarts on every card; it resets while held. With reduced motion it is full.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Continue to video". Goes to step 15.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ---------- Screen 15 -->
<h3>Screen 15: What are instructions? (<code>/module?step=15</code>)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Shell</td><td>With the blue <code>wash</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Heading</td><td>"What are <i>instructions</i>?" as karaoke text. Words timed 0.49-0.76, 0.76-1.12, 1.12-1.72 s of <code>screen_6_audio.mpeg</code> (only the first 2.15 s plays: <code>#end=2.15</code>).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sub text</td><td>"Watch this short video to understand instructions with real examples." (16 px, <code>#666666</code>).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Video card</td><td>340 x 309 px thumbnail (<code>video-thumbnail-new.png</code>, 8 px radius) with a soft <b>cyan glow</b> behind it: <code>#79DDFF</code> at 24% with a 75 px blur. A white 69 px play circle (border <code>#F0F0FF</code>, shadow <code>1px 1px 13.2px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.25)</code>) with a teal play icon sits at the centre; press scales to 0.95 and plays the click sound.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Player bar</td><td>48 px bar at the bottom of the card, black 65% with a 3.35 px backdrop blur: play icon, 00:00, a track (<code>#818185</code>) with a green knob (<code>#01A17F</code>), 02:45, fullscreen icon. This is a static mock (the video does not play).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Note box</td><td>Lavender tinted box <code>#B286FD</code> at 11%: sparkles icon, divider, bold "In this video," and "We will tell that in programming what instructions really known as."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Continue". Goes to step 16.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ---------- Screen 16 -->
<h3>Screen 16: Let's guide Hex (<code>/module?step=16</code>)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Mini game: walk Hex to the battery. Go Straight wins; Go Back loses and offers a retry. Graded (first go counts).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Title</td><td>"Let's <i>guide</i> Hex" (one line).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Background</td><td><b>MeadowBackdrop</b>: <code>guide-hex-bg.webp</code> (3:2, at least 803 px wide) centred, with a white wash <b>gradient</b> over it: white 45% at the top, 60% at 55%, solid white at the bottom (lighting that fades the meadow into the button area).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Platform</td><td><code>guide-hex-platform.webp</code>, 356 x 266 px, at Figma top 216. A 3 x 3 board; only the middle column is used: top, centre, bottom tiles at 18.3%, 47.5%, 76.6% of the height.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Battery</td><td>66 x 60 px battery icon standing on the top tile with a <b>yellow radial glow</b> (<code>rgba(255,226,70,0.85)</code> fading to transparent at 70%) 20 px beyond the icon. When solved, it scales to 0 and fades in 0.2 s (collected).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hex</td><td>Starts on the centre tile. Moves with a spring (stiffness 320, damping 30) to the tile chosen. Box 100 px, lifted 10 px so he stands on the tile.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Buttons</td><td>Two 3D buttons (150.5 x 99 px, 18 px apart) at Figma top 508: <b>Go Straight</b> (light blue <code>#EDFAFE</code>, edge <code>#BFE6F2</code>, blue gradient up arrow) and <b>Go Back</b> (cream <code>#FEF8EC</code>, edge <code>#F2DFB8</code>, orange gradient arrow flipped down). Each face stands 4 px up on a darker edge and sinks onto it when pressed (100 ms). They are disabled once Hex has left the centre.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sound</td><td><code>step</code> blip on each move.</td></tr>
<tr><td>After 400 ms (Go Straight)</td><td><code>win</code> sound + haptic, battery collected, <b>Gem popup</b> opens (see below), Continue enabled. <b>When the popup closes</b> (tap, or its 3 s countdown), the battery is claimed: <b>+1 unit, every time Hex reaches the battery</b>, and the full-screen <b>Battery Doctor</b> (<code>BTRY-005_HEX_Battery_Doctor</code>) plays over the screen; when it ends the header battery flashes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>After 400 ms (Go Back)</td><td><code>lose</code> sound + haptic. First miss is noted as wrong for review. A <b>red result panel</b> slides up: "Oops, that's the wrong way! The battery is straight ahead. Tap anywhere on this panel to try again." Button becomes "Try again". Tapping the panel or the button resets Hex to the centre and re-enables the buttons.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Continue</td><td>Disabled until a result exists. On the solved path it notes the answer (right if never missed) and goes via <code>nextAfter</code> to review or complete.</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>Gem popup (<code>GemPopup</code>)</h4>
<ul>
  <li>Dark overlay (<code>bg-black/45</code>, 0.25 s fade). Card 356 x 494 px, 32 px radius, springs in (scale 0.85 &rarr; 1, y 24 &rarr; 0, stiffness 260, damping 22) and exits with scale 0.92.</li>
  <li>Content: "+10 XP" orange (32 px), the gem with burst image, "Congratulations!", a mint chip with the gem (tilted -19.9 degrees) and "1 Gem", a sparkle divider, and "You won 1 Gem as you followed the given command."</li>
  <li><b>Countdown bar</b> along the bottom (6 px, teal) drains left to right over 3 s (linear); the popup closes itself at 3 s. Tap anywhere or the X to close early (click sound).</li>
</ul>

<!-- ===================================================== 6 -->
<h2>6. Review intro screen (<code>/module?step=review</code>)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>When</td><td>After step 16 when at least one graded question was answered wrong the first time. If nothing is missed (for example link or reload with the answers gone) it redirects to complete.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Progress bar</td><td>Full at step 16 with the total increased by the number of questions to redo.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Layout</td><td>Hex (190 px box) at the top.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Text</td><td>Title "Let's fix the ones you <i>missed</i>" drops in from 24 px above (spring 140 / 16, delay 0.3 s). Body "N questions to go again. Keep going until you get every one right." (or "1 question") fades up 16 px in 0.4 s, delay 0.5 s.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Let's go" - starts the review queue and goes to the first missed step. Back goes to <code>/level</code>.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ===================================================== 7 -->
<h2>7. Lesson complete screen (<code>/module?step=complete</code>)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Display</td><td>Full-screen Rive artboard <code>LESSON_Complete</code> (from <code>hex.riv</code>), fit width, held to 430 px wide and centred on a desktop. No header.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Values written</td><td>Once ready, the artboard's data is set: <b>XP +40</b>, <b>accuracy</b> (first try percentage), <b>time 3:42</b> (222 s, fixed value). Written as numbers, or as strings ("+40", "92%", "3:42") if the artboard declares strings. Then the <code>play</code> trigger fires the celebration.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Haptic</td><td>One long 1.2 s vibration.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>"Continue" (module button, full phone width). It saves module 1 as finished (<code>completeModule</code>), resets review and streak, and returns to <code>/level</code> where Hex moves to the next block.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ===================================================== 8 -->
<h2>8. Timing and constants cheat sheet</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>What</th><th>Value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Title spring</td><td>stiffness 140, damping 16, delay 0.15 s, from y -24</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cards enter</td><td>opacity 0.3 s, y spring 110/13, delay 0.3 s, from y 90</td></tr>
<tr><td>Result panel spring</td><td>stiffness 360, damping 32 (also drives cards rising 180 px, picture crop, Hex sinking)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hex typing</td><td>350 ms start delay, 55 ms per character</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hex exit follow</td><td>80 ms after bubble; bubble 0.15 s, Hex 0.2 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hex ambient idle</td><td>every 4 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Panel Hex enter</td><td>250 ms after sheet; cue after 900 ms; cue plays about 2.8 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button press</td><td>hold 150 ms, onClick at 330 ms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Button shine</td><td>every 5 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Electric effect</td><td>0.67 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Strike delay</td><td>150 ms after correct/wrong</td></tr>
<tr><td>Robot move gap</td><td>150 ms + clip length; first move 600 ms after load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hint fill</td><td>0.8 s; float 2.4 s loop; flip 1.2 s x 2 turns</td></tr>
<tr><td>Match: wrong shake / release</td><td>0.28 s / 300 ms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Match: right lift / grey</td><td>1.2 s / 540 ms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Examples carousel</td><td>3.6 s auto, 0.9 s move</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gem popup</td><td>3 s auto close</td></tr>
<tr><td>Move Hex result delay</td><td>400 ms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Out-of-energy delay</td><td>600 ms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Confetti</td><td>120 pieces, gravity 0.35</td></tr>
<tr><td>XP burst</td><td>1.6 s, "+10 XP", 56 px</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Colour palette</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Use</th><th>Colour</th></tr>
<tr><td>Brand teal / gradient</td><td><code>#04ACAB</code>, gradient <code>#00B8A9</code> &rarr; <code>#1387B3</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Body text</td><td><code>#444444</code> (headings on some screens <code>#2C2C2C</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Correct</td><td>panel <code>#E3F6F3</code>, border <code>#7FD8CC</code>, title <code>#01A17F</code>, card fill <code>#F2FBF8</code>, edge <code>#008566</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Wrong</td><td>panel <code>#FDECEC</code>, border <code>#D42421</code>, card border <code>#E5484D</code>, fill <code>#FFF1F1</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Hint / XP orange</td><td><code>#FF8D42</code> (hint), fill <code>#FFE7D1</code>, XP <code>#F5A623</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Match selected blue</td><td>border <code>#5B9BFF</code>, fill <code>#EEF4FF</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Speech bubble edge</td><td><code>rgba(18,140,179,0.5)</code></td></tr>
</table>

